{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/16120-what-to-do-with-melkor","id":16120,"title":"What to do with Melkor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-22T08:50:12-08:00","id":16120,"title":"What to do with Melkor","content":"So I'm tenatively putting together Tolkien's Valar and Maiar as a Pantheon, and I keep hitting a dead end as to what to do with Eru Illuvatar and Melkor. One of them is going to be the Titan, probably Melkor, but I like keeping him around as the token evil god in the bunch....<br /> Although I could just promote Sauron to that position, and have Melkor be the Titan who escaped the Doors of Night.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts to help me figure this out would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:25:09-08:00","id":16132,"title":"","content":"Why don't you keep Melkor as the &quot;evil guy&quot; of the Pantheon (like Loki in the Aesir) and in a curious twist keep Eru Illuvatar as the Titan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:42:26-08:00","id":16140,"title":"","content":"I only had this as a reference point:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://tolkiengateway.net/w/images/0/00/Merp_lords1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <i>The Black Enemy's most fundamental desire, of course, was to create life. Yet, he never could, for the Imperishable Flame burns only within Eru, and life abides only with the leave of the One. Even the birth of Aule's Dwarves can be traced to Eru's forgiving thought. Morgoth was always frustrated in his endeavor to find and wield the fire that kindles the spirit and sparks life.<br /> <br /> Still, Morgoth held the power to pervert that which was, and his breeding pits produced the races of Orcs, Trolls, Wargs, and Dragons, as well as a host of foul denizens which still haunt the depths of the Earth. He seduced the Fire Spirits and twisted their souls, yielding the awful Demons of Might; the Balrogs. On a still grander scale, he implanted the seeds of pride and despair that changed the very outlook on life.<br /> <br /> Morgoth was a master of many aspects of Ea, but above all he enjoyed a command of crafts and material things. He was after all closest in mind and character to Aule</i><br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> &quot;He hated light...and would have attacked the Moon had his strength not failed him.&quot;<br /> <br /> well then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:19:43-08:00","id":16162,"title":"","content":"How about just saying Melkor is a token evil god and ignoring the Titan War entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:28:45-08:00","id":16169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/16120-what-to-do-with-melkor?p=16132#post16132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't you keep Melkor as the &quot;evil guy&quot; of the Pantheon (like Loki in the Aesir) and in a curious twist keep Eru Illuvatar as the Titan?</div> </div> </div> </div>During my afternoon nap, I saw Eru as a manifestation of Light. After Aten assumed control of the Greater Titan of Light by murdering all the other avatars, the Valar released Melkor for added muscle.<br /> The Great Enemy is siding with his brothers, but only for the sake of avenging Eru, and the loss of the Flame Imperishable. He really, really wanted that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/16120-what-to-do-with-melkor?p=16162#post16162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about just saying Melkor is a token evil god and ignoring the Titan War entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another possibility. If it's not the default time, like during the Middle Ages or even during WWII, the titans haven't escaped yet. I could use Melkor and the Valar as the are in the Silmarillion, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:41:19-08:00","id":16173,"title":"","content":"Or you could do it in the modern era, having realized that needing a group of designated antagonists is bollocks that does nothing but arbitrarily butcher existing mythology.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though WWII would be a pretty good time for a LotR/The Hobbit Campaign. Mostly because that was about the time Tolkien was writing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}